      "writtenOn": "2020-07-31T22:00:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The thing is we should even be doing retries in the TPMC because the tRetry timer that we should use when we don\u0027t get a response is actually 195 usec, and we have no hope for TCPM in the loop on those retrys. I didn\u0027t realize this was in the spec.\n\nCheck out Section 6.6.1 in PD spec specifically tRetry.\n\nI think we completely made up the TCPC_TX_TIMEOUT time. I couldn\u0027t find that in the spec anywhere.",
      "parentUuid": "fcc78c6f_81a9aea0",
      "revId": "093dc24947efe13f0960f298aa3b93576b06ff1f",
